WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.620
Speaker 1: So public health officials were
starting to worry about this about six weeks

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:11.880
ago, and we worried we were likely about a
month away around mid-March and it's apparently

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:12.880
happening.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.750
We are now seeing a slowdown in vaccinations,
not because of the temporary pause on the

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:23.760
Johnson and Johnson vaccine expected to resume
very soon, not because of the lack of vaccine

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:30.660
supply, not because of a lack of appointments
or a lack of vaccinators, as Joe Biden likes

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:31.660
to say.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:38.329
But because supply is starting to exceed demand
for the vaccine in some of the more anti vaccine

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:45.100
strongholds, by which I mean mostly in twenty,
twenty one Republican areas where 43 percent

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:52.501
of the country's Republicans said at last
week's polling date they do not plan, nor

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:57.609
are they interested in getting the coronavirus
vaccine all over the country.

00:00:57.609 --> 00:01:03.109
We are hearing about vaccine vaccination centers
with wide open appointments, even simply walk

00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:04.109
in.

00:01:04.109 --> 00:01:07.560
People were telling me in Mississippi it was
just come and walk in.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.689
In Massachusetts, it was just simply come
and show up with no appointment.

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:17.680
In California, in some cases, vaccines going
unused, appointments going unfilled.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:23.140
There are currently two hundred and seventy
seven million vaccines that have been distributed,

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:28.510
but only two hundred and fifteen million vaccines
that have been administered, meaning that

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:36.329
states are now sitting on 62 million doses
with more coming in on a regular basis.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:43.259
Now, some of those 62 million are reserved
second doses for states that are still going

00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:45.229
about it in that way.

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:47.070
But this is not a great sign.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:54.310
Overall, we right now, as of yesterday, have
about 26 percent of the population fully vaccinated

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:58.759
and 40 percent has received at least one dose.

00:01:58.759 --> 00:02:05.439
But the number of doses given has declined
to just about three million doses per day.

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:11.000
We had multiple days in the last week with
under two million doses per day given, which

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.410
is a reversal of the direction that things
were going.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.660
We can crush this thing.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.440
We actually have the tools, the resources
and the vaccine supply to crush this thing

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.190
if we keep vaccinating quickly, more quickly.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.920
But instead, vaccination is slowing down.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.440
It may be temporary.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.220
We know that about 20 percent of the country
overall doesn't want a vaccine.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.730
Overwhelmingly, that group is Republicans.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.880
As I mentioned, 43 percent of Republicans
do not want the vaccine.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.000
That's going to hurt our ability to fight
this.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:46.850
And the very people who from the beginning
have said they want this over or at least

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.410
they want to act like it's over.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.160
Well, we have a way to make it be over.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.250
And it's called getting vaccinated.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:55.090
But 43 percent of them don't want the vaccine.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.430
That's going to hurt our ability to fight
this.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:03.160
Now, one great thing that Joe Biden announced
yesterday is a tax credit for employers to

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.740
offer paid leave to workers to go and get
vaccinated.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.130
We're going to talk about this more on the
bonus show.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:13.490
Joe Biden tweeting, quote, I believe everyone
who wants the vaccine should be able to get

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.490
one.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:20.430
Today, I announced the tax credit made possible
by the American rescue plan to help employers

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:24.360
offer paid leave to workers getting vaccinated.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.840
You can learn more at IRS dot gov covid.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:35.130
As things continue to open and the odds of
needing a vaccine to go certain places increases

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:38.800
that will probably encourage more people to
get vaccinated.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:43.630
But understand that at this point it's not,
oh, how could we may be ended?

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.110
When could the end be in sight?

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:51.310
We could very quickly get to the pandemic
end game and of course in the fall we already

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:55.990
know there will likely be boosters for tailored
to the variants.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:59.910
But as far as what we can do now to have a
very normal Fourth of July, just two and a

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:05.580
half months from now, to have a relatively
OK Memorial Day just five weeks from now,

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:09.370
if we keep vaccinating more quickly, we can
do it again.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:14.450
Look at what's happening in Israel, where
56 percent of the country is fully vaccinated.

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:15.659
It's not 70 percent.

00:04:15.659 --> 00:04:20.980
It's not 80 percent, with 56 percent fully
vaccinated in Israel.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:25.450
Cases are so low that it almost looks like
zero on the chart that we are looking at,

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:28.340
it's actually about 140 cases per day.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:31.330
The this is just the perfect example.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:36.050
Israel and New Jersey have the same size and
the same population.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:39.850
You look up geographic area for Israel and
New Jersey, it's almost the same.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:42.190
You look at population, it's almost the same.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:45.120
New Jersey has 4000 cases a day.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.130
Israel has 140 just stunning.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:53.890
And its vaccines deaths also, by the way,
approaching zero in Israel, about six per

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.140
day right now.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.850
For comparison, New Jersey is averaging about
40 deaths a day.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:02.610
Seven times the deaths in New Jersey than
in Israel.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:07.290
Same population, same geographical size, and
it is vaccines.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:11.710
If we can just stay at three million doses
a day, we're still going to look pretty good

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:12.980
in four to five weeks.

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:16.080
If we can get to four million doses a day,
it'll be even faster.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.360
Now, if we go back to two million doses a
day or even one point six, one point five

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:25.340
million, we give the variants more opportunity
in time to spread.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.500
We prolong this.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.000
Let's not do that, OK?

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.600
Full eligibility for adults right now in every
state.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.950
Very, very simple.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:07:04.570
Just get yourself vaccinated, then figure
out whether you can convince somebody else

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:16.699
to 

00:07:16.699 --> 00:07:24.449
do it.

